'' RUN: '@' of a string literal is a 'zstring ptr' to the literal's bytes -- through an
'' iif, a macro's '@(lit)', parentheses, a string constant and adjacent literals. tiko
'' typed it 'string ptr' (spurious TKO0833, a crashing 'var', the wrong overload) and
'' lowered '@("abc")' to a one-character string. Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/addr-of-literal.bas -o tests/codegen/addrofliteral.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0833
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0830
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/addrofliteral.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/addrofliteral.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: cz:wb
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: cz:rb
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: z:macro
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: z:konst
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: z:nskonst
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: z:adjacent
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: z:parens
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: v:var len 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ov zstring ptr
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: assign
